WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.979
Modern organizations generate enormous amounts of security-relevant information.

2
00:00:04.979 --> 00:00:14.059
Firewalls, servers, cloud platforms, endpoint tools, identity providers, applications, and network devices all produce logs.

3
00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:19.387
Each source can tell part of the story, but none of them gives complete visibility by itself.

4
00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:22.660
Reviewing these logs manually is nearly impossible.

5
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.820
Important warning signs may be buried among millions of normal events.

6
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:36.090
A suspicious login, firewall deny, endpoint alert, and cloud configuration change may matter more when viewed together than when reviewed separately.

7
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:45.878
SIEM platforms help organizations collect, organize, and analyze this information so security teams can identify suspicious activity more effectively.

8
00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:52.353
SIEM exists because defenders need visibility across many systems rather than isolated pieces of information.
